{"title":"2021 AIME I Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Piecewise_Function:_Analysis_and_Graph)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Piecewise Function: Analysis and Graph)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b10a3d88db47a7d7dc0b6c5b26b32aac2e94e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left||20|x|-x^2|-c\\right|=21\\]\" width=\"169\" height=\"22\" />has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinct real solutions.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Piecewise_Function:_Analysis_and_Graph.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Piecewise_Function:_Analysis_and_Graph)\">Solution 1 (Piecewise Function: Analysis and Graph)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Piecewise Function: Analysis and Graph)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We take cases for the outermost absolute value, then rearrange: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7ff936bc1efa460cb60cd0e89204c19c39419d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|20|x|-x^2\\right|=c\\pm21.\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"22\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1b45d4cecf8f2c2604f759bafdfffa2ccc41c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\left|20|x|-x^2\\right|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"156\" height=\"22\" /> We rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> as a piecewise function without using absolute values:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a582536815a665c1495b906ababc042dcaf6e37d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = \\begin{cases} \\left|-20x-x^2\\right| &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x \\le 0  \\begin{cases} 20x+x^2 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x\\le-20 \\\\ -20x-x^2 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ -20&lt;x\\leq0 \\end{cases} \\\\ \\left|20x-x^2\\right| &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x &gt; 0 \\begin{cases} 20x-x^2 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ 0&lt;x\\leq20 \\\\ -20x+x^2 &amp; \\mathrm{if} \\ x&gt;20 \\end{cases} \\end{cases}.\\]\" width=\"499\" height=\"107\" />\nWe graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97eded22ccc3e54189a8f157c4e81f36fe034a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> with all extremum points labeled, as shown below. The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is an even function (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ecc7adaba484954946c18ad202a289eae6809a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> holds for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> so the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97eded22ccc3e54189a8f157c4e81f36fe034a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is symmetric about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis) should facilitate the process of graphing.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48503ab7aa27c5858d43d018cc0f91c669b8ee93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(1200,300);   real xMin = -65; real xMax = 65; real yMin = -50; real yMax = 125;  draw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2));  real f(real x) { return abs(20*abs(x)-x^2); } real g(real x) { return 21; } real h(real x) { return -21; } draw(graph(f,-25,25),red,&quot;$y=\\left|20|x|-x^2\\right|$&quot;); draw(graph(g,-65,65),blue,&quot;$y=\\pm21$&quot;); draw(graph(h,-65,65),blue);  pair A[]; A[0] = (-20,0); A[1] = (-10,100); A[2] = (0,0); A[3] = (10,100); A[4] = (20,0);  for(int i = 0; i &lt;= 4; ++i) { dot(A[i],red+linewidth(4.5));  }  label(&quot;$(-20,0)$&quot;,A[0],(-1.5,-1.5),red,UnFill); label(&quot;$(-10,100)$&quot;,A[1],(-1.5,1.5),red); label(&quot;$(0,0)$&quot;,A[2],(0,-1.5),red,UnFill); label(&quot;$(10,100)$&quot;,A[3],(1.5,1.5),red); label(&quot;$(20,0)$&quot;,A[4],(1.5,-1.5),red,UnFill);  add(legend(),point(E),40E,UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"678\" height=\"502\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48f6dc55891156675c1ba2d390f27be32ee8f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=c\\pm21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinct real solutions, it is clear that each case has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct real solutions geometrically. We shift the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cab5989cb9cccd3e3109b25c5b5d574ade0d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\pm21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> units, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec468aa5866edc73304535b21b7bc8e102750d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\geq0:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a27d21ab87f2ec62a5207209832f0a36f3a37e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=c+21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct real solutions, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea611d53bd24bb118f2f0e5a470425116a6f17ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq c&lt;79.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01fb23845acf973c0dd580acfb9f2429132ec22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=c-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct real solutions, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b4839afb3532905088be06a2c78132496a5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21&lt;c&lt;121.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"12\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Taking the intersection of these two cases gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7dee88897ae47dd01c957759766cdf9e2834fb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21&lt;c&lt;79,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> from which there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8efb5737dc876e3e57168b0ecab0e4c8393f59b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$79-21-1=\\boxed{057}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"23\" /> such integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201a2eef545643b50b07fed5c09e894bcced5c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c.$\" width=\"11\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Graphing)\">Solution 2 (Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe332497d54334e32722973fe0ef2488b24830f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|20|x|-x^2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"19\" /> (If you are having trouble, look at the description in the next two lines and/or the diagram in Solution 1). Notice that we want this to be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad36609ff5314d7d3748122b7e9f6015b74c4949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5d19d504a21d8688357ac6ad7988ce63bbb78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We see that from left to right, the graph first dips from very positive to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d98445b749e2d24fad986a665b750f93699b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-20$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />, then rebounds up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/17059fbed4499b422fc8cb388e92c20e457edf97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, then falls back down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are symmetric, so the graph re-ascends to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec186fd1809357d1f530bee2334ceb59d405b4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, falls back to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec186fd1809357d1f530bee2334ceb59d405b4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, and rises to arbitrarily large values afterwards.\n</p><p>Now we analyze the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (varied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />) values. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a58dc80839ca93d0749124afaea7681ae478b9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=k&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, we will have no solutions, as the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27c522cab00176729dcb425293b1be0276f6b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> will have no intersections with our graph.\n</p><p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we will have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions for the three zeroes.\n</p><p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/1389e2659f2768e57520a30bfad43ab342fa8d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, we will have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beade0a93199527f8d91f3d69c4045b199268ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions, because local maxima are reached at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf6fd4efa7e4845d580cb91fc23428b7465bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\pm 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2221242e688931114bb23b8c785b0b95dff9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=m&gt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />, we will have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>To get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinct solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fa1e02c5735667a1992af05afcfdc271d97588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=|20|x|-x^2|=c \\pm 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63eb48fc42209c13b9622cce5c31bb8dce4b3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c +21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad36609ff5314d7d3748122b7e9f6015b74c4949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> must produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b31800ef8e365fb9191d9a0455c330eea2659e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;c-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52cdfed552c6a811343e8205d61db1b81e4c88d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+21&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c580b0876f6a8c2b5b276515829bdc3bd1b5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in \\{ 22, 23, \\dots , 77, 78 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" /> is required.\n</p><p>It is easy to verify that all of these choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> distinct solutions (none overlap), so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2ff12404524ee07bca13d0aae660df80a2eb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{057}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Graphing)\">Solution 3 (Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/60892eb0f812b664996878290648437bed93797d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = |x|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> Then the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8e8324826264c68bae64af8574b15222afd4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\left|20y-y^2\\right|-c\\right| = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"162\" height=\"22\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/8031a252a415f3541d56739ec401c972d39b659e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|y^2-20y\\right| = c \\pm 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1088ea966adc3199481765ec5227eed20173cf52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = |x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is nonnegative, so we only care about nonnegative solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that each positive solution in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gives two solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46351223dc154e9ccfaee76b939c91bf3140ec28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />), whereas if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is a solution, this only gives one solution in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Since the total number of solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is even, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> must not be a solution. Hence, we require that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/8031a252a415f3541d56739ec401c972d39b659e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|y^2-20y\\right| = c \\pm 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive solutions and is not solved by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/7917cfec5119aab77bad2dc6754225400bdfd50f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/16434c0b60482b218128c7c11db64191eae96b74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb335299681e7b35789b5f758d2a9e0873660ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c - 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> is negative, and therefore cannot be the absolute value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356439396721fd71bb1790b3e6fb272c1f7bca0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 20y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. This means the equation's only solutions are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/21494576263fb186241467f8b333bb6482f84ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|y^2-20y\\right| = c + 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"22\" />. There is no way for this equation to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions, since the quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/2261f26e0fc2e7ff83fea565c90c4ef0e8d87df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-20y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> can only take on each of the two values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb6ab13baf714a7ab6dd2eb0c5fa6eb0250e66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm(c + 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> at most twice, yielding at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f448347c277e5eb0dc829665e9049370f56d96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> also can't equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, since this would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> would solve the equation. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/8/05888dc1d0d92db8915ccac5fc7ecaa98d5afef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; 21.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>At this point, the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab41167a74f3921276f44e6ddac9abf18af28e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-20y = c \\pm 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> will always have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> positive solutions, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/2261f26e0fc2e7ff83fea565c90c4ef0e8d87df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-20y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> takes on each positive value exactly once when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is restricted to positive values (graph it to see this), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36b724053dca2b4dabd32a143491b8406975c68f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\pm 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> are both positive. Therefore, we just need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976fd40d62836a96b6deec1a2d928af24d8fec12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-20y = -(c \\pm 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" /> to have the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions exactly. This means the horizontal lines at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831a16dacb57b6174c6eeb9e5a3d62ecfe525fdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(c \\pm 21)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> each intersect the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/356439396721fd71bb1790b3e6fb272c1f7bca0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 20y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> in two places. This occurs when the two lines are above the parabola's vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/68905f768f59a814b412bd914517df3392f8e0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,-100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. Hence we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92de30a93a54d2860525f70e29388d85a41e733.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -(c + 21) &amp;&gt; -100 \\\\ c + 21 &amp;&lt; 100 \\\\ c &amp;&lt; 79. \\end{align*}\" width=\"139\" height=\"64\" />\nHence, the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the conditions are those satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c00cdf0fef64a50bc8e4c3bc304373d00a9bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 &lt; c &lt; 79.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" /> There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2ff12404524ee07bca13d0aae660df80a2eb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{057}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> such integers.\n</p><p>Note: Be careful of counting at the end, you may mess up and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe61e5b80572ad5a200a0d9cd354ce12a8c7800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Algebra)\">Solution 4 (Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Removing the absolute value bars from the equation successively, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffdbe4fb0afddf7ef8bf63e2aeedc2a6024b8d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left|\\left|20|x|-x^2\\right|-c\\right|&amp;=21 \\\\ \\left|20|x|-x^2\\right|&amp;= c \\pm21 \\\\ 20|x|-x^2 &amp;= \\pm c \\pm 21 \\\\ x^2 \\pm 20x \\pm c \\pm21 &amp;= 0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"224\" height=\"99\" />\nThe discriminant of this equation is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10a2a5919655517de0dd7e6519ec41450447dd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{400-4(\\pm c \\pm 21)}.\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"32\" />\nEquating the discriminant to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we see that there will be two distinct solutions to each of the possible quadratics above only in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f7c20a3676c61720ca55287e5e659eab8fb309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-79 &lt; c &lt; 79$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />. However, the number of zeros the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d695abd65942ca73e25ea4cc16fada6b32fd4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+b|x|+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> has is determined by where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2ff4c7f1f82267c9ff123cb9d8de09d6e999d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+bx+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0974c2843c614f0129302a1b0c29a0896eba97d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2-bx+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> intersect, namely at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0658fa5f64bbe8fbe318420d63186079e262dc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e6630318d8cb28de2723180b6d359b972489c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d695abd65942ca73e25ea4cc16fada6b32fd4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+b|x|+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> will have only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b043119262a2beb49176cb4beb5c50ec1915a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> real solutions, if they exist at all.\nIn order to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> solutions here, we thus need to ensure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffecfa0d2fc4098513c5fff87080a3de90071828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-c+21&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" />, so that exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> out of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible equations of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d695abd65942ca73e25ea4cc16fada6b32fd4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2+b|x|+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> given above have y-intercepts below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> real solutions, while the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equations have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions. This occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/652269ab74c0e0fb384b1ac19af460bf462cf6b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, so our final bounds are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff6852a91cb90c5bf4637755511898e0903a13e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21&lt;c&lt;79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2ff12404524ee07bca13d0aae660df80a2eb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{057}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> valid values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b6658679cc5bf8b3b2e75f0418e1b770c362f83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x)=\\left||20|x|-x^2|-c\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"191\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616636bda6ca5508030a41deed662ce3a39be8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G(x)=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> are shown here in Desmos: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.desmos.com/calculator/i6l98lxwpp\">https://www.desmos.com/calculator/i6l98lxwpp</a>\n</p><p>Move the slider around for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff6852a91cb90c5bf4637755511898e0903a13e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21&lt;c&lt;79$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> to observe how they intersect for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6k-uR71_jg0\">https://youtu.be/6k-uR71_jg0</a>\n~mathproblemsolvingskills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I\" title=\"2021 AIME I\">2021 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2021 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2021\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n<